      "text": "To determine the fraction of items on the menu that I can eat, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of items on the menu.\n2. Determine the number of items that do not contain meat.\n3. Determine the number of vegetarian dishes that do not contain gluten.\n4. Calculate the fraction of items that I can eat.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the Total Number of Items on the Menu\n\nWe know that there are 4 meatless dishes, which represent one fifth of the menu. Let's denote the total number of items on the menu by \\( T \\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{5} T = 4 \\]\n\nTo find \\( T \\):\n\\[ T = 4 \\times 5 = 20 \\]\n\nSo, the total number of items on the menu is 20.\n\n### Step 2: Determine the Number of Items That Do Not Contain Meat\n\nSince there are 4 meatless dishes and they are one fifth of the menu, the total number of items on the menu is:\n\\[ T = 5 \\times 4 = 20 \\]\n\nThus, the total number of items on the menu is 20.\n\n### Step 3: Determine the Number of Vegetarian Dishes That Do Not Contain Gluten\n\nWe are given that 3 of the meatless dishes are gluten-containing (made with pasta). Therefore, the number of gluten-free meatless dishes is:\n\\[ 4 - 3 = 1 \\]\n\nThere is only 1 gluten-free meatless dish. We also need to check if other non-meat items are available.\n\n### Step 4: Calculate the Fraction of Items That I Can Eat\n\nBased on the above information, we can summarize the types of items I can eat:\n- Eating meat exceeds this criterion, so I cannot eat any dishes with meat.\n- Only 1 of the 4 meatless dishes has gluten.\n- All items listed as vegetarian can be eaten. \n\nTo find the total number of items I can eat:\n\\[ 20 - 1 = 19 \\]\n\nThus, the total number of items I can eat is 19.\n\nFinally, the fraction of items on the menu that I can eat is:\n\\[ \\frac{19}{20} \\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{19}{20}}\n\\]",
